# Netlify redirects. Rules are matched top to bottom. vercel.json carries the
# same list for Vercel (the host in use); keep the two in step.

# Every address of the old hyltansmetall.se (its sitemap, Nov 2026), so links
# and search results pointing at them land on the matching new page. 301 =
# moved for good, which also tells Google to move the ranking over.
# /, /produkter/, /produkter/anglar, /produkter/tomtar and /specialtillverkning
# kept their addresses.
/om-foretaget                         /om-oss          301
/tillverkningen                       /tillverkning    301
/kontakta-oss                         /kontakt         301
# Old product categories with no page of their own on the new site.
/produkter/till-kyrka-och-forsamling  /produkter       301
/produkter/ovriga-produkter           /produkter       301
/produkter/tavlor                     /produkter       301
/produkter/malmklockor                /produkter       301
# Malmljusstakar comes back at this same address once its hidden flag is
# removed, so only a temporary redirect (302) until then. Netlify serves an
# existing file before a rule like this, so the published page takes over by
# itself; on Vercel the redirect in vercel.json must be deleted.
/produkter/malmljusstakar             /produkter       302

# No catch-all rewrite to index.html: every page is prerendered to its own
# file (scripts/prerender.mjs), which Netlify serves for /om-oss from
# om-oss.html. Anything else gets dist/404.html with a real 404 status.
